  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Below normal temperatures continue through Saturday. \n\nA cool dry airmass will remain in place as high pressure over the \nGreat Lakes moves east-southeast through Friday. The center of \nthe surface high will move over northern New York tonight. \nMostly clear skies and light winds will provide a favorable \nsetup for radiational cooling. Low temperatures will be from \nthe lower to mid 30s across the interior portions east of Lake \nOntario and the interior Southern Tier, and upper 30s and lower \n40s across western New York. A Frost Advisory is in effect for \nthe eastern Lake Ontario region and Allegany county tonight \nwhere sensitive vegetation may be harmed if not protected. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Widespread soaking rain Friday night into Saturday \nnight.\n\nA wave of low pressure will move into the Great Lakes along an \nadvancing warm front from the Ohio Valley Friday night and \nSaturday. This will bring a period of widespread, soaking rain \nalong with possible embedded thunderstorms. A deep southerly flow\nahead of the surface low will advance northward across the Ohio\nValley, as the warm front approaches western New York. Warm air\nadvection and increasing moisture will result in showers \nstarting to move into western New York Friday night. \n\nA shortwave trough will catch up with the surface low over the Ohio \nValley, spreading widespread moderate to heavy rain across western \nNew York Saturday. A strong area of high pressure over the Canadian \nMaritimes is expected to maintain mostly dry conditions east of Lake \nOntario. Enhanced rainfall is possible across western New York \nwhere a strong low-level jet interacts with a very moist airmass.\nUncertainty exist in the exact location of the enhanced rainfall,\nbut instability will be limited in this environment, however a \nfew embedded thunderstorms are possible. \n\nThe upper level ridge and surface high will move east Saturday night \nwhile large scale ascent and moisture will move into the eastern \nGreat Lakes region. Showers will continue across western New York\nwhile spreading into north-central New York. The current forecast\nincludes rainfall amounts of 1.0-1.5\" across western New York \nand 0.25-0.75\" across the Eastern Lake Ontario region Friday night\nthrough Saturday night. This amount of rainfall has the potential\nto cause ponding and minor flooding of low lying areas. Rises \non rivers and creeks is expected, with a few possibly reaching\naction stage, but widespread flooding is not expected.",
